From a076f6a582cd60b7a7d12d711aec3022661a635b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(pathkernel): the ring and row guide planners

K2, first part (#4176): the guide stage of the path kernel gets its
ring planner and its row planner behind GuidePlanner, and Guides sends
each guide choice to its family's planner (the medial line and the
trace are refused by name until the second part).

- Rings are the level sets of the distance to the walls (Held 1991),
  spaced by the choice's stepover; RingRef::Part rings stop at the
  stock edge. Clean-up rings cover what the regular rings leave; the
  0.1 mm2 guard makes the result incomplete with each gap named.
- A full-width stretch (#3788) is named with a mark that K3 and K4
  read: the tool disc overlaps no disc of the next deeper curves and
  no air.
- Rows run at the angle, evenly spaced at the stepover or less, clipped
  to the centre area, with a closing ring on request.
- Small pieces are kept; every refusal is a named const.

Pins: the laws suite (guide_rings, guide_rows) and the motion pins in
pass_start_levels/kernel_rings.rs against the recorded old rings.
No old planner changes.

Refs #4176

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
