From 74766eaa57edc0cd6ab220b7dcf46164b764cfcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:23:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(pathkernel): name each dropped mark; pin closing
 rings and open-ring marks

Review of PR #4189, findings 2 to 4:
- 2: nothing that a planner made is dropped without a note. When the
  curve checks refuse a raw curve, its note also names the marks on it
  that are not kept (unit pin a_refused_curve_names_its_marks_in_its_note).
- 3: the closing ring of a rows choice runs round each loop of the area,
  an island included (pin the_closing_ring_of_rows_runs_round_each_island_too).
- 4: a full-width stretch on an open ring round a part is named (pin
  a_full_width_stretch_on_an_open_ring_round_a_part_is_named).

Refs #4176

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/pathkernel/src/guide/cover.rs        | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/guide_guard.rs | 19 +++++++++++++--
